{
  "_readme": [
    "Owner-editable routing table: product category x destination region -> ordered supplier candidates.",
    "Format and precedence: web/COMMERCE_ARCH.md section e. Edit, redeploy, done. No code change is needed.",
    "candidates: tried in order. An inner list [\"a\", \"b\"] is a tier of equals: the cheaper landed cost wins, then the faster one.",
    "An EMPTY list means: not sold in that region. \"manual\" means: sell it and let a person place the supplier order by hand.",
    "Source: the routing table of the supply study (reports, section 'jadwal al-tawjih'). Only suppliers with an adapter are listed (Printful, Printify, Gelato, Printlet); Prodigi, Contrado, Art of Where and Teelaunch are left out.",
    "Every cell the study marks as unconfirmed, 'test order first' or 'after catalogue check' is EMPTY on purpose: all of GCC, most of AE, drinkware and wall art in EG, stationery and engraved in EU and UK. Add the supplier here after a successful test order.",
    "AE apparel and phone cases: the study's first choice (Gelato) is unconfirmed and 'Printful global' is only a last resort with possible duties at the door, so the cell stays empty until the owner decides.",
    "blocked: categories that are never sold online (perfume and electronics are deferred by the study).",
    "costFx: rough conversion to EUR, used ONLY to compare supplier costs with each other. Never used for customer prices.",
    "In mock mode (COMMERCE_MODE=mock) the mock supplier stands in for every supplier named here."
  ],
  "version": 1,
